entry.summary:
I built pistachio, a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL. You write the schema you want in SQL, and the CLI generates the DDL diff against the current database and applies it in a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow. CREATE TABLE public.users ( id integer NOT NULL, name text NOT NULL, email text NOT NULL, -- added this line CONSTRAINT users_pkey PRIMARY KEY (id) );
Add that one line to the schema file, and: $ pista plan schema.sql -- Connected to postgres://postgres@localhost/postgres -- Plan for schema public (1 table, 0 views, 0 enums, 0 domains, 0 composite types, 0 sequences) ALTER TABLE public.users ADD COLUMN email text NOT NULL;
$ pista apply schema.sql -- Connected to postgres://postgres@localhost/postgres -- Apply to schema public (1 table, 0 views, …
